    {
      "id": "13613",
      "body": "User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 : few questions just to make sure I’m correctly capturing Contentful requirements:\n\n1. **Contentful content type.** The Client Services contact details / supporting copy will be fetched from Contentful. Do I need to create a user story for this Contentful component, or will this be done as part of Contentful scope?\n1. **Empty cart heading.** Should \"YOUR BAG IS EMPTY\" be hardcoded in the PWA component, or should it be managed in Contentful?\n1. **Contentful fetch failure behaviour** (AC6): What's the expected behaviour when a Contentful fetch fails or content hasn't been authored? Is there a global pattern for this across the PWA we should reference?",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
        "name": "Isabel Chaloner",
        "email": "isabel.chaloner@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e5a0df80fa413e572a441e3890e6a12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FIC-6.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-03T11:11:47.476+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-03T11:16:13.742+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13618",
      "body": "User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc, thanks, definitely good questions!\n\n1. Looking at the design, is it safe to assume that this information will changed based on which storefront they’re on? I’m guessing it would and we may want to ask the business if the Google Business data is the master and we rely on that, or if it is something they want to author independntly.\n  1. Also, this would likely be a simple ‘text’ content model which we can fetch via the Contentful API\n1. Yeah, this is similar to the hardcoded labels question I asked Transperfect last week, we’ll likely create a ‘placeholders’ content model in Contentful for labels like these\n1. Yeah there will be a global behaviour, it would not render that content and come back as an empty string.\n\nAlso User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc  - Looking at this story, I would seperate out the Empty Cary and Einstein as seperate stories/components. Ideally,\n\n- We have an Epic for Cart and all the cart related stories live under that Epic.\n- We have an Epic for Einstein as that will need to be it’s own component as that component will likely live on multiple pages.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "name": "Tim Lavelle",
        "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
