{"result":"{
  "id": "19324",
  "key": "SFCC-825",
  "summary": "Cart – Populated Cart State: Component Render Order & Logic",
  "description": "As a Shopper, I want to see all my bag contents clearly organised when my cart contains items, so that I can review my selections and proceed to checkout.\n\nThis story covers the logic of when the populated cart state is triggered and the render order and scroll behaviour of all components within the cart drawer. It does not cover the build of any individual component — each has its own dedicated story. This is the populated cart equivalent of the empty cart state logic story (SFCC-277).\n\n**Desktop Layout:**\n\n  - **TOP: Cart Drawer Container (SFCC-315)* — the outer drawer that renders the full populated cart state.\n  - **(RHS) Cart Summary Component (SFCC-816)* — remains fixed/sticky as the Shopper scrolls through cart items on desktop\n  - **(LHS) Page-level notification banner (SFCC-404)* — sticky, displayed at the top when applicable\n  - **(LHS) Product container* — contains all cart item cards (SFCC-795). This is not a standalone component — it is a scrollable container that groups all cart items together. The scroll behaviour of the entire cart is dictated by this container:\n      - If there are 3 or fewer items, the full cart including Zimmermann Benefits is visible without scrolling\n      - If there are more than 3 items, the product container is cropped — the Shopper scrolls within the left-hand side to reveal additional items. The cart summary component remains sticky on the right throughout\n      - Once the Shopper has scrolled to the end of the product list, the whole page scrolls and Zimmermann Benefits becomes visible\n  - **BOTTOM:* Zimmermann Benefits (SFCC-317) — visible once the Shopper has scrolled past all cart items.\n\n**Mobile / Tablet Structure:**\n\n- The entire screen scrolls as a single page — there is no split sticky/scrollable layout. All components stack vertically and the Shopper scrolls through the full cart in one continuous scroll.\n\n*UI Kit:* [https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=40000257-6983&p=f&t=V3wHXdHkDiGTFYDY-0](https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026) \n\n*Designs:*\n\n![\"image-20260827-055955.png\"](image-20260827-055955.png)",
